    <string name="info_mot_title">Annual Vehicle Inspection (MOT / Test)</string>
    <string name="info_mot_desc">Every vehicle in Israel is required to pass an annual safety inspection (Test/MOT) to drive on public roads. New vehicles up to 3 years old are exempt, vehicles aged 3 to 19 require an annual inspection, and vehicles over 19 years old require an inspection twice a year along with a classic/aging vehicle garage certificate.</string>
    <string name="info_safety_title">Safety Equipment Rating (0-8)</string>
    <string name="info_safety_desc">The official safety rating is determined by the Ministry of Transport based on active safety systems installed in the vehicle (such as autonomous emergency braking, lane keep assist, blind-spot monitoring, adaptive cruise control, and more). Higher scores indicate more advanced safety equipment.</string>
    <string name="info_emission_title">Emission Groups (1-15)</string>
    <string name="info_emission_desc">Air pollution green groups range from 1 to 15, where group 1 represents fully electric zero-emission vehicles, and group 15 includes vehicles with high emission levels. The pollution group directly impacts purchase tax and annual licensing fees.</string>
    <string name="info_disabled_app_title">Disabled Parking Permit Check App</string>
    <string name="info_disabled_app_desc">A dedicated lightweight app for real-time verification of disabled parking permits. Ideal for quick on-site checks in parking lots and streets.</string>
